````markdown name=docs/Fineract-DEX-Integration-Plan-2025-11-30.md
# Fineract ↔ DEX Integration Plan — 2025-11-30

Status: Draft  
Prepared by: (fill)  
Related repos: apache/fineract, Direct-Private-Offers/dpo-dex

## Summary
Purpose: Outline how the DEX (dpo-dex) will integrate under the Fineract umbrella (accounts, compliance, ledger) and provide a concrete set of tasks and artifacts to implement integration.

## Key findings (to be filled by GH AI scan of both repos)
- Fineract modules relevant:
  - Accounts / ledgers
  - Transactions / settlements
  - Audit & event logging
  - Access control & roles
- DEX components relevant:
  - Swap endpoints and contracts
  - Liquidity pool management
  - Token models and identifiers
  - Event streams (on-chain events if any) and off-chain services

## API Mapping
- Fineract endpoints (fill after scan):
  - GET/POST /accounts
  - POST /transactions
  - GET /ledger/entries
  - ...
- DEX endpoints (fill after scan):
  - POST /swap
  - GET /pools
  - POST /liquidity/add
  - ...
- Suggested alignment:
  - Map DEX swap -> Fineract transaction with fields: {accountId, externalAssetId, amount, counterparty, metadata}
  - Use consistent id mapping: token contract address -> externalAssetId; maintain cross-reference table in Fineract.

## Data model mapping
- Fineract model examples:
  - Client: {clientId, name, identifiers}
  - Account: {accountId, accountType, ledgerId}
  - Transaction: {transactionId, debitAccount, creditAccount, amount, currency, timestamp}
- DEX model examples:
  - Token: {tokenId (contract address), symbol, decimals}
  - Swap: {swapId, fromToken, toToken, amountIn, amountOut, timestamp}
  - LiquidityPool: {poolId, tokens[], reserves[]}
- Mapping table (example row)
  - DEX token.contractAddress ↔ Fineract externalAssetId
  - Swap.swapId ↔ Transaction.transactionId (or ledger entry reference)

## Event flows (text diagram)
Fineract (Umbrella)
  ├─ Ledger / Accounts / Audit
  ├─ Compliance service
  └─ Integration adapter (REST / queue)
        ↕
DEX Service (dpo-dex) — Swap API / on-chain listeners
        ↕
PSP rails / Settlement

Label integration points:
- API call: DEX swap -> Fineract integration adapter POST /transactions
- Ledger sync: After successful swap, adapter writes ledger entry in Fineract
- Reconciliation: Periodic job compares DEX on-chain state with Fineract ledger

## Integration tasks and priorities (conservative estimates)
1. Create integration adapter service (REST + queue) — Medium
   - Accept DEX swap webhooks, map to Fineract transaction, call Fineract API
2. Asset mapping table in Fineract — Small
   - Maintain mapping from token contract -> externalAssetId
3. Audit logging hook — Small
   - On every mapped swap, append audit entry to Fineract audit tables
4. Reconciliation job (daily) — Medium
   - Fetch on-chain or DEX state and reconcile with ledger
5. End-to-end tests and security review — Large
   - KYC/AML checks, role-based access, signing, rate-limits

## Sample request / response examples
- Example: DEX sends swap webhook (example)
  POST /integration/dex/swap
  {
    "swapId": "0xabc...",
    "fromToken": "0xTokenA",
    "toToken": "0xTokenB",
    "amountIn": "1000000000000000000",
    "amountOut": "490000000000000000",
    "userAccount": "user-123",
    "timestamp": "2025-11-30T12:34:56Z"
  }
- Integration adapter -> Fineract POST /transactions (example)
  {
    "transactionReference": "dex-swap-0xabc...",
    "debitAccountId": "fineract:wallet:user-123:TokenA",
    "creditAccountId": "fineract:wallet:liquidity-pool:TokenA",
    "amount": "1.0",
    "currency": "TokenA",
    "metadata": { "dexSwapId": "0xabc..." }
  }

## Deployment (sample docker-compose)
```yaml
version: '3.8'
services:
  fineract:
    image: apache/fineract:latest
    ports: ['8080:8080']
    environment:
      - DB_HOST=postgres
  dpo-dex:
    image: dpo-dex:latest
    ports: ['3000:3000']
  integration-adapter:
    build: ./integration-adapter
    environment:
      - FINERACT_BASE_URL=http://fineract:8080
      - DEX_BASE_URL=http://dpo-dex:3000
    depends_on:
      - fineract
      - dpo-dex
  postgres:
    image: postgres:13
    environment:
      - POSTGRES_PASSWORD=change-me
    volumes:
      - pgdata:/var/lib/postgresql/data

volumes:
  pgdata:
```

## Compliance & Audit Hooks
- On each mapped swap:
  - Create audit record: {eventType: "DEX_SWAP", actor, timestamp, details}
  - Record actor identity: map wallet <> Fineract client (KYC link)
  - Store raw DEX event payload in an append-only audit store
- Role-based access:
  - Only integration-adapter service account has write access to transaction endpoints
  - Use service tokens and IP allowlist for extra control

## Tests & Validation
- Unit test: mapping logic for token decimals and amounts
- Integration test: end-to-end swap -> ledger write -> audit entry
- Reconciliation test: simulated out-of-sync detection and repair flow

## Next steps and backlog (short)
1. Run automated GH AI prompts against both repos and fill “Key findings” + exact endpoints and models.
2. Implement integration-adapter skeleton (1–2 days).
3. Implement asset mapping table and admin UI (1 day).
4. Implement audit hook and tests (1–2 days).
5. Security review and E2E tests (3+ days).

## Appendix
- Links:
  - Fineract repo: https://github.com/apache/fineract
  - DEX repo: https://github.com/Direct-Private-Offers/dpo-dex
- (Add extracted endpoints, file references, and code locations here after scans.)
````

````markdown name=docs/README.md
# docs/ — docx generation & instructions

This folder contains integration prompt and plan markdown files. Two docx files are desired:
- docs/A_B_Testing.WIP9-FineractDEXIntegrationPrompts-2025-11-30.docx
- docs/Fineract-DEX-Integration-Plan-2025-11-30.docx

If DOCX conversion is not done automatically, you can generate locally using pandoc.

Local pandoc example (install pandoc first):
- Convert a single file:
  pandoc docs/A_B_Testing.WIP9-FineractDEXIntegrationPrompts-2025-11-30.md -o docs/A_B_Testing.WIP9-FineractDEXIntegrationPrompts-2025-11-30.docx

- Convert and include a table of contents:
  pandoc --toc docs/Fineract-DEX-Integration-Plan-2025-11-30.md -o docs/Fineract-DEX-Integration-Plan-2025-11-30.docx

GitHub Action to convert on push (example workflow: .github/workflows/md-to-docx.yml)
```yaml
name: Convert MD to DOCX
on:
  push:
    branches:
      - DPO.Finetrac

jobs:
  convert:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
      - name: Install pandoc
        run: sudo apt-get update && sudo apt-get install -y pandoc
      - name: Convert prompts
        run: |
          pandoc docs/A_B_Testing.WIP9-FineractDEXIntegrationPrompts-2025-11-30.md -o docs/A_B_Testing.WIP9-FineractDEXIntegrationPrompts-2025-11-30.docx
          pandoc --toc docs/Fineract-DEX-Integration-Plan-2025-11-30.md -o docs/Fineract-DEX-Integration-Plan-2025-11-30.docx
      - name: Commit converted files
        run: |
          git config user.name "github-actions"
          git config user.email "actions@github.com"
          git add docs/*.docx
          git commit -m "Add generated DOCX files" || echo "No changes to commit"
          git push origin DPO.Finetrac
```

Notes:
- Ensure the workflow has permission to push to the branch (set the workflow to run on branch DPO.Finetrac or open a pull request from the branch).
- If using a fork-based workflow, check token permissions for push.
````

