````markdown name=docs/Fineract-DEX-Integration-Plan-2025-11-30.md
# Fineract ↔ DEX Integration Plan — 2025-11-30

Purpose
- Enable Direct-Private-Offers/dpo-dex (DEX) to operate as a subordinate, pluggable service under Apache Fineract’s umbrella architecture.
- Define concrete integration points, data-model mappings, event flows, audit/RBAC hooks, deployment example, and a prioritized task list.

High-level stance
- Fineract = umbrella architecture: canonical source of clients, accounts, ledgers, compliance, settlements, and audit trails.
- DEX = component/service: token/pair/pool management, swap execution, on-chain/off-chain listeners, and user wallet integration.
- Integration pattern: lightweight integration adapter(s) that translate DEX events into Fineract transactions/journal entries and ensure compliance/audit.

1) Fineract core modules (summary)
- Clients
  - Persistent KYC/KYB records, party identifiers (externalIds, legal identifiers such as LEI).
  - Client lifecycle management.
- Accounts
  - Account objects (savings, checking, wallets, externalAsset-linked accounts).
  - Ledger-backed balances and accounting integration.
- Portfolio
  - Product definitions, accounts grouped by client/product.
- Payments & Settlements
  - REST endpoints to initiate and settle transactions, settlement batches, external rails adapters.
- Compliance
  - KYC/AML checks, rules engine, flags, holds, sanctions screening.
- Audit & Logging
  - Append-only audit records, immutability patterns, who/when/what for financial entries.
  - Transaction trails and reconciliation interfaces.

2) DEX repo core modules (summary)
- Tokens
  - Token metadata (contract address, symbol, decimals, metadata, off-chain identifiers).
- Pairs / Pools
  - Liquidity pools, reserves, pool tokens, pool identifiers.
- Swaps
  - Swap engine (price math, slippage, routing), swap endpoints and transaction receipts.
- Wallet integration
  - User wallet binding, signature flows, private-key/user account mapping (often off-ledger).
- Event listeners
  - On-chain event watchers (SwapExecuted, LiquidityAdded/Removed), webhook emitters.
- Admin & Metadata
  - Token registration, pool lifecycle management, fee configuration.

3) REST endpoint inventory & suggested alignment
Note: exact file/route names vary by repo. Below are canonical endpoints to extract and align.

Fineract (canonical endpoints to locate/use)
- Clients
  - GET /clients
  - GET /clients/{clientId}
  - POST /clients
- Accounts
  - GET /accounts/{accountId}
  - POST /accounts (create account/wallet)
  - GET /accounts?clientId={id}
- Transactions / Ledger
  - POST /transactions (create financial transaction)
  - GET /transactions/{transactionId}
  - GET /journalentries or /ledgers (ledger queries)
- Settlements / Batches
  - POST /settlements
  - GET /settlements/{id}
- Audit
  - GET /audit/records
- Authentication/Service Accounts
  - OAuth/service-token endpoints or API-key usage for service-to-service calls

DEX (common endpoints to map)
- Tokens & Metadata
  - GET /tokens
  - POST /tokens/register
- Pools / Pairs
  - GET /pools
  - POST /pools/create
- Swaps
  - POST /swap (request a swap)
  - GET /swap/{swapId}/status
- Liquidity management
  - POST /liquidity/add
  - POST /liquidity/remove
- Webhooks / Events
  - POST /webhooks (to register)
  - emits swap, liquidity, pool events

Suggested API alignment (patterns)
- DEX swap -> Fineract transaction:
  - DEX emits a webhook on swap finalization: POST /integration/dex/swap
  - Integration adapter translates swap -> POST /transactions in Fineract, storing dexSwapId in metadata.
- Token registration -> Asset record:
  - When a token is registered in DEX, adapter creates/updates an externalAsset record in Fineract (mapping token contract address -> externalAssetId).
- Liquidity events -> Journal entries + audit:
  - Liquidity adds/removes create corresponding ledger journal entries, plus a stored audit payload for reconciliation.
- Reconciliation endpoints:
  - Periodic jobs in Fineract call DEX endpoints (GET /pools, GET /swaps?since=) for reconciliation.

4) Data-model mapping (concise)

Fineract models (examples)
- Client
  - { clientId, externalIds: [LEI, otherIds], name, kycStatus }
- Account
  - { accountId, clientId, accountType, currency, externalAssetId?, ledgerId }
- Transaction
  - { transactionId, debitAccountId, creditAccountId, amount, currency, timestamp, metadata }
- JournalEntry
  - { journalEntryId, ledgerId, entries: [{accountId, debit, credit}], timestamp }

DEX models (examples)
- Token
  - { tokenId (contract address), symbol, decimals, metadata, identifiers: {ISIN?, externalId?} }
- Pair / Pool
  - { poolId, tokenA, tokenB, reserves: {reserveA, reserveB}, lpToken }
- Swap
  - { swapId, poolId, fromToken, toToken, amountIn, amountOut, userWallet, txHash, status, timestamp }

Identifier mapping (ISIN, LEI, UTI)
- LEI (Legal Entity Identifier)
  - Map LEI -> Client.externalIds for any counterparty organizations (market makers, liquidity providers).
- ISIN (Security Identifier)
  - If token represents a regulated security, store ISIN as Token.identifiers.isin and mirrored in Fineract external asset metadata.
- UTI (Unique Transaction Identifier)
  - Use UTI for cross-system transaction correlation: populate Transaction.metadata.uti = dexSwap.uti or generate UTI at integration adapter time.
- Recommended canonical fields
  - Fineract externalAsset: { externalAssetId, tokenContractAddress, symbol, ISIN?, issuerLEI? }
  - Link: Token.tokenId (contract) ↔ externalAsset.externalAssetId

5) Text-based event flow diagram (top-down)
Fineract (Umbrella)
  ├─ API: /transactions, /accounts, /clients, /audit
  ├─ Integration Adapter (service)
  │     ├─ POST /integration/dex/swap  <--- DEX webhook
  │     ├─ GET /integration/dex/pools   <--- periodic reconciliation
  │     └─ Calls -> Fineract POST /transactions, POST /journalentries
  ├─ Compliance Service (KYC/AML)
  └─ Audit Store

DEX (Component)
  ├─ REST API: /swap, /pools, /tokens
  ├─ On-chain Listeners -> emits events
  └─ Webhook -> Integration Adapter

PSP / External Exchange (Rails)
  ├─ Settlement endpoints
  └─ Settlement adapter <-> Fineract Settlement module

Integration points (labels)
- API calls: DEX webhook -> Integration adapter -> Fineract /transactions
- Ledger sync: adapter writes JournalEntry/transaction; reconciliation job compares DEX on-chain state -> ledger
- Compliance hooks: adapter queries Compliance service before posting high-value swaps (KYC/AML)
- Audit: adapter stores raw DEX payload + mapping record in Fineract audit store

6) Audit logging & RBAC — how to capture DEX events
- RBAC pattern
  - Create a dedicated service account for integration-adapter with a minimal scope: create transaction, create audit record.
  - Limit write permissions to the adapter’s client credentials, enforce IP restrictions and rotate keys.
- Audit logging pattern
  - On every adapter action that writes a transaction, also create an audit record:
    - Audit record fields: { eventType: "DEX_SWAP"|"DEX_LIQUIDITY", actor: "integration-adapter", clientId, dexSwapId, rawPayload, timestamp, result, correlationId }
  - Store rawPayload as compressed JSON in append-only audit table/blob store to preserve forensic data.
- Capture chain-of-custody
  - Add correlationId/UTI to both DEX swap and Fineract transaction.
- Reconciliation & alerts
  - Periodic reconciliation job that compares DEX events/chain-state with Fineract ledger; generate mismatch alerts and remediation flows (replay, repair).
- Retention & compliance
  - Keep audit records per regulatory retention (configurable), exportable for regulators.
- Example flow
  1. DEX emits SwapExecuted webhook -> adapter.
  2. Adapter validates KYC via Fineract Compliance service.
  3. Adapter writes Transaction into Fineract, writes JournalEntry, and creates Audit record with raw DEX payload.
  4. Adapter returns acknowledgment to DEX; DEX marks swap finalized.

7) Sample request/response examples

DEX -> Integration Adapter (webhook)
```http
POST /integration/dex/swap
Content-Type: application/json
{
  "swapId":"0xabc123",
  "poolId":"pool-0x01",
  "fromToken":"0xTokenA",
  "toToken":"0xTokenB",
  "amountIn":"1000000000000000000",
  "amountOut":"495000000000000000",
  "userWallet":"0xUserWallet",
  "txHash":"0xchainTx",
  "timestamp":"2025-11-30T12:34:56Z",
  "metadata": { "routing": ["pool-0x01"], "slippage":"0.5%" }
}
```

Adapter -> Fineract (create transaction)
```http
POST /transactions
Authorization: Bearer <integration-service-token>
Content-Type: application/json
{
  "transactionReference": "dex-swap-0xabc123",
  "debitAccountId": "fineract:wallet:0xUserWallet:TokenA",
  "creditAccountId": "fineract:pool:pool-0x01:TokenA",
  "amount": "1.0",
  "currency": "TokenA",
  "metadata": { "dexSwapId":"0xabc123", "dexTxHash":"0xchainTx", "uti":"UTI-2025-11-30-0001" }
}
```

8) Sample docker-compose (minimal)
```yaml
version: '3.8'
services:
  fineract:
    image: apache/fineract:latest
    ports:
      - "8080:8080"
    environment:
      - SPRING_PROFILES_ACTIVE=default
      - DB_HOST=postgres
    depends_on:
      - postgres

  dpo-dex:
    image: dpo-dex:latest
    ports:
      - "3000:3000"
    environment:
      - NODE_ENV=production
      - WEBHOOK_URL=http://integration-adapter:4000/integration/dex/swap

  integration-adapter:
    build: ./integration-adapter
    ports:
      - "4000:4000"
    environment:
      - FINERACT_BASE_URL=http://fineract:8080
      - DEX_BASE_URL=http://dpo-dex:3000
      - SERVICE_TOKEN=change-me
    depends_on:
      - fineract
      - dpo-dex

  postgres:
    image: postgres:13
    environment:
      - POSTGRES_PASSWORD=change-me
    volumes:
      - pgdata:/var/lib/postgresql/data

volumes:
  pgdata:
```

9) Task breakdown & priorities (estimates)
- 1. Discover & map exact endpoints and model classes in both repos — Small (0.5 day)
  - Produce exact file references and examples.
- 2. Implement integration-adapter skeleton (webhook receiver, mapper, Fineract client) — Medium (1–2 days)
- 3. Asset mapping table in Fineract (externalAsset records) + admin UI — Small (1 day)
- 4. Audit record schema + persistence of raw DEX payload — Small (0.5–1 day)
- 5. Reconciliation job (periodic) + reporting — Medium (1–2 days)
- 6. End-to-end tests (swap -> ledger -> audit -> reconcile) — Large (3+ days)
- 7. Security review, RBAC, secrets rotation, and monitoring — Large (3+ days)

10) Recommendations & next steps
- Run the GH AI prompts against both repos to extract exact endpoint/filename references (controllers, route files, model classes) and paste outputs here or grant read access.
- Implement a small integration-adapter service in a separate repo/folder with:
  - Webhook receiver
  - Fineract client (service-token based)
